BE-300 2.4.18: make serial_be300 usable as an interactive ttyS0.

The linux4be serial_be300 driver registered a tty, but it never fully
programmed the UART as a Linux console/getty device.  The most visible
bug was be300_set_baud() leaving UART_LCR_DLAB set after writing the
divisor, so later writes to UART_TX could update the divisor latch
instead of transmitting bytes.  The driver also ignored termios, never
asserted RTS, and depended on an IRQ path that is not wired for the
VRC4173 companion UART in this 2.4 port.

Program ttyS0 as 115200 8N1, clear DLAB after divisor updates, assert
DTR|RTS so the emulator's VRC4173 SIU bridge sees the guest as ready,
and poll RX into the tty flip buffer.  This keeps the default Opie build
on framebuffer console tty0 while allowing ttyS0::askfirst:/bin/sh to be
used through --serial1-bridge pty:auto.

